\"https:\/\/www.linkedin.com\/in\/ashimajain90\/\"],\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/author\/ashima\/\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716552880103\",\"position\":1,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716552880103\",\"name\":\"Does meta description affect search rankings?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Meta title and meta descriptions are not search engine ranking factors and Google announced the same. However, they can affect a page\u2019s click-through rate, which can influence its ranking in SERPs. Meta titles and meta descriptions can promote your web page and compel them to click on the link. When a searcher visits the page, they can evaluate if the content is useful and valuable for them and answer their queries. Basically, meta title and meta description are not primary search ranking factors but can affect a page\u2019s ranking by influencing user behavior. Therefore, make sure you create engaging and attractive meta descriptions for your page.\u00a0\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716552897910\",\"position\":2,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716552897910\",\"name\":\"What should I write in a meta description?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Your meta description must include a compelling and interesting summary of the page content so searchers click on it. It should convey what they can find when they visit the page and include relevant keywords so search engines can index the page and rank it.\u00a0\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553016305\",\"position\":3,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553016305\",\"name\":\"Where can I see meta descriptions in HTML?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"When you open the page source, you can see the meta description under the &lt;head> section of the HTML markup. You can edit this markup and modify the meta description within the code or the meta description field within the page\u2019s metadata settings.\u00a0\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1739980821359\",\"position\":4,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1739980821359\",\"name\":\"What is a pixel limit for meta titles?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The pixel limit for a meta title is approximately 580\u2013600 pixels wide.\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553030915\",\"position\":5,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553030915\",\"name\":\"How does the meta description appear in SERPs?\",\"answerCount\":1,\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"You can see meta descriptions in SERPs as a part of a web page snippet, just under the clickable title and breadcrumb path.\u00a0\",\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en-US\"},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553048090\",\"position\":6,\"url\":\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553048090\",\"name\":\"Should every web page have a meta description?\