 Basically, meta title and meta description are not primary search ranking factors but can affect a page\u2019s ranking by influencing user behavior. Therefore, make sure you create engaging and attractive meta descriptions for your page.\u00a0","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716552897910","position":2,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716552897910","name":"What should I write in a meta description?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Your meta description must include a compelling and interesting summary of the page content so searchers click on it. It should convey what they can find when they visit the page and include relevant keywords so search engines can index the page and rank it.\u00a0","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553016305","position":3,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553016305","name":"Where can I see meta descriptions in HTML?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"When you open the page source, you can see the meta description under the &lt;head> section of the HTML markup. You can edit this markup and modify the meta description within the code or the meta description field within the page\u2019s metadata settings.\u00a0","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1739980821359","position":4,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1739980821359","name":"What is a pixel limit for meta titles?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The pixel limit for a meta title is approximately 580\u2013600 pixels wide.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553030915","position":5,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553030915","name":"How does the meta description appear in SERPs?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can see meta descriptions in SERPs as a part of a web page snippet, just under the clickable title and breadcrumb path.\u00a0","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553048090","position":6,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553048090","name":"Should every web page have a meta description?\u00a0","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, it\u2019s important that every web page has a meta description. However, make sure that these descriptions are not identical or similar, as they are not good. Also, it can affect your CTR, which is nad for traffic and ranking. If you don\u2019t write a meta description for any of the web pages, Google will use a random part of your content to create one and display it in SERPs. This description may not be relevant to the content and hamper user experience.\u00a0","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553072464","position":7,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/meta-title-description-length\/#faq-question-1716553072464","name":"What are some good meta description generator tools?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A few top meta description generator tools are Ahrefs, Dashword, Rytr, Copysmith, AISEO, and Writesonic.\u00a0","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@